details:
(a) the total number of teacher vacancies in Government elementary and secondary schools as of mid-2026, with particular reference to rural, tribal and educationally backward districts across States;
(b) the current status of recruitment processes under Samagra Shiksha and various State drives and the main reasons for persistent delays in filling sanctioned posts despite multiple announcements; and
(c) the impact of prolonged teacher vacancies on pupil-teacher ratios, multi-grade teaching and learning outcomes, especially for students from marginalised and economically weaker sections?

(a) details of stretches of National Highways and Expressways damaged due to heavy rainfall, landslides, flooding or erosion during the current southwest monsoon season 2026, including States most affected;
(b) the funds allocated and utilized for emergency repairs, restoration and traffic management on affected highways; and
(c) steps taken to improve drainage systems, slope protection and adoption of climate-resilient designs in highway projects to reduce future monsoon-related disruptions, accidents and inconvenience to the public?

(a) the latest data on school dropout rates at elementary, secondary and higher secondary levels for the academic year 2025-26, including State-wise variations and trends among girls, SC, ST and minority students;
(b) the effectiveness of measures such as vocational education, bridge courses and financial incentives introduced under NEP 2020 and Samagra Shiksha in reducing dropouts; and
(c) whether any States have reported an increase in dropouts linked to implementation challenges of the new curriculum, examination patterns or structural changes under the National Education Policy, particularly affecting the new academic session starting in 2026?

(a) the number of claims received, approved, rejected and pending under Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) as of mid-2026, along with the major reasons for claim rejections;
(b) the current status of hospital empanelment under the scheme, particularly in rural and semi-urban areas and reports of denial of treatment or additional charges being levied on eligible beneficiaries; and
(c) the steps taken to address delays in claim settlement and to reduce out-of-pocket expenditure for scheme beneficiaries in light of grievances received from States and patients?

(a) details of funds allocated and utilized for maintenance and repair of National Highways during Financial Year 2025-26 and the first quarter of Financial Year 2026-27;
(b) reports of poor construction quality, premature deterioration, potholes and accidents on recently constructed or upgraded National Highways and action taken against defaulting contractors; and
(c) the mechanism for independent quality audits and public grievance redressal regarding the condition of National Highways across the country?

(a) the progress made in introducing four-year undergraduate programmes, multidisciplinary education and other National Education Policy, 2020 structural changes across higher education institutions as of mid-2026, including resistance, delays or implementation gaps reported from various states;
(b) the progress in curriculum revision, introduction of vocational subjects and new assessment patterns under NEP, 2020 at school level, and their reported impact on teaching quality and student learning as per recent surveys; and
(c) measures taken to address the digital divide in rural, marginalised and economically weaker sections for effective rollout of the new education framework, and any reported adverse effects on students from these backgrounds?

(a) the number of cases of dengue, malaria, chikungunya and other vector-borne diseases reported across the country during the current southwest monsoon season 2026 as compared to the corresponding period in 2025, along with reported fatalities;
(b) the status of preparedness measures such as fogging operations, larvicide spraying, availability of hospital beds, medicines and diagnostic kits in high-risk States and districts; and
(c) whether any States have reported shortages or sought additional central assistance for outbreak control and the reasons for any delays in response measures particularly affecting vulnerable populations in urban slums and rural areas?

(a) the percentage of Primary Health Centres (PHCs) and Community Health Centres (CHCs) that are fully functional with adequate staff, equipment, medicines and diagnostic facilities as per Indian Public Health Standards as on date;
(b) the extent of shortage of doctors, specialists and paramedical staff in rural health facilities across States; and
(c) the measures taken to strengthen 24×7 emergency services, obstetric care and diagnostic facilities in underserved rural areas?

(a) the details of improvement in productivity in pulses and oilseeds under the ongoing self-sufficiency mission, till date;
(b) the extent to which climate-resilient seed varieties have been adopted by farmers in 2025; and
(c) the steps taken to ensure remunerative prices and reduce post-harvest losses in light of recent Budget priorities?

(a) the details of incentives disbursed under the Production Linked Incentive (PLI) schemes for key sectors like electronics and automobiles during financial year 2025-26 till date;
(b) whether domestic manufacturing capacity has increased in these sectors as per targets set in 2025; and
(c) the steps taken to address supply chain vulnerabilities highlighted in the Economic Survey 2025?

(a) the status of employment generation and export growth achieved under the Production Linked Incentive (PLI) schemes for electronics, automobiles and pharmaceuticals sector till December 2025;
(b) whether any sectors have met or exceeded their domestic value addition targets under these schemes; and
(c) the challenges faced in supply chain localization and measures taken to address them?

(a) the trends in out-of-pocket expenditure on healthcare by beneficiaries under Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) in the last two years;
(b) the number of hospitals empanelled and claims settled in rural vs, urban areas as of January 2026; and
(c) any plans to address gaps in coverage for chronic illnesses?

(a) the latest unemployment rate among youth (15-29 years) as per Periodic Labour Force Survey;
(b) the placement rates achieved under major skill development programmes in 2025; and
(c) the plans to align skilling initiatives with emerging sectors like AI and green jobs?

(a) the current installed capacity of solar and wind energy as of December 2025 and challenges in meeting the 2030 targets;
(b) the status of pilot projects under the National Green Hydrogen Mission; and
(c) the measures to accelerate private investment in renewable energy storage and transmission infrastructure?

(a) the number of formal jobs created in the organised sector during 2024-25 and the first half of 2025-26, as per EPFO and ESIC data;
(b) whether the unemployment rate among youth aged 20–29 years has shown any decline in the latest Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS) quarterly bulletin; and
(c) the details of skill development programmes launched or expanded during 2025 under the Skill India Mission?

(a) the total length of national highways constructed during April–October, 2025; 
(b) the number of highway projects currently under litigation or facing land-acquisition delays; and
(c) the revised timeline for completion of the Delhi–Mumbai Expressway and the Bharatmala Pariyojana Phase-I?

(a) the number of active COVID-19 cases and vaccination coverage rates across the country as of November 1, 2025;
(b) the preparedness level of Government for any potential resurgence of respiratory illnesses during the winter season, including stock of essential medicines; and
(c) the details of new public health campaigns launched in 2025 to promote booster doses among high-risk groups?

(a) the current storage levels in the 150 major reservoirs of the country as on 15th November, 2025 compared to the levels on the corresponding date in 2024;
(b) whether any States are facing acute water shortage for Rabi sowing this year; and
(c) if so, the details thereof and the Central assistance provided under the Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) and Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (PMKSY) to the affected States?

(a) the total export figures for the month of October 2025 and the cumulative exports during April–October, 2025–26; 
(b) whether exports of electronics, pharmaceuticals and engineering goods have registered growth over the corresponding period of the previous year; and
(c) if not, the sectors which have shown decline and the corrective steps taken by Government to achieve the export target of US$ 800 billion set for Financial Year 2025-26?

(a) the Minimum Support Price (MSP) fixed for major Rabi crops for the 2025-26 season; 
(b) the extent of crop damage due to unseasonal rains in October 2025 in major wheat-producing States like Uttar Pradesh and Madhya Pradesh; and 
(c) the details of relief packages announced under the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) for affected farmers, including claims processed till date?

(a) the current status of air quality in the National Capital Region (NCR), as of October 2025, including the average AQI levels in Delhi and its satellite cities;
(b) the steps Government has initiated under the National Clean Air Programme (NCAP) to reduce stubble burning incidents in the States of Punjab and Haryana during the 2025 Kharif harvesting season; and
(c) the details of funds allocated and utilized under NCAP for NCR States during the year 2024-25 and 2025-26?

(a) the enrollment ratio in Higher Education Institutions (HEIs) for the academic year 2025-26, as compared to 2024-25; 
(b) the number of new seats created under the National Education Policy (NEP), 2020 in multidisciplinary education and research Universities during 2025; and 
(c) the measures being taken to address the digital divide in rural areas for online learning access?

(a) the manner in which Government has countered claims of India-Pakistan hyphenation in global diplomacy;
(b) the diplomatic measures taken by Government to address China’s growing influence over Pakistan in terms of intelligence and military cooperation; and
(c) the manner in which Government plans to strengthen India’s foreign policy narrative in 2025-2026?

(a) whether progress has been made on implementing the National Education Policy (NEP), 2020, and how will its goals be supported in 2025-2026;
(b) the NEP 2020 milestones the Ministry has achieved by July, 2025;
(c) the NEP initiatives, the Ministry is prioritizing for implementation in 2025; and
(d) how will the Ministry address NEP implementation challenges by 2026?

(a) the specific measures taken by Government to address unemployment in rural areas, and the manner in which job creation will be enhanced under schemes like Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) in 2025-2026;
(b) the data collected by the Ministry on rural unemployment trends in 2025;
(c) the new MGNREGS projects launched by the Ministry to boost rural employment; and
(d) the manner in which the Ministry will assess job creation outcomes under MGNREGS by 2026?

(a) the countries which have been engaged for intelligence-sharing following the all-party delegation;
(b) the protocols being implemented to secure shared intelligence with international partners; and
(c) the manner in which the Ministry will assess the benefits of global intelligence cooperation in 2025 and beyond?

(a) the measures Government is implementing to address prison overcrowding and the progress made since 2024;
(b) the details of prison overcrowding across States as of year 2025;
(c) what prison reform initiatives has the Ministry launched since 2024; and
(d) how will the Ministry monitor progress on prison overcrowding in 2025-2026?

(a) what measures are in place to enhance renewable energy adoption, particularly solar and wind, in line with the country's climate goals for 2030;
(b) the current solar and wind energy capacity reported by the Ministry in 2025;
(c) the incentives offered by the Ministry for adoption of renewable energy in 2025; and
(d) the manner in which the Ministry will track the progress toward 2030 climate goals?

(a) the progress that has been made on the Smart Cities Mission (SCM), and the manner in which urban infrastructure will be improved in 2025-2026;
(b) the key achievements Ministry has recorded for the SCM by 2025;
(c) which urban infrastructure projects is the Ministry prioritizing in 2025; and
(d) the manner in which the Ministry will assess urban infrastructure improvements by 2026?

(a) the details of funds spent for renovation/construction of various airports in the country which were privatized during the last five years; 
(b) the reasons for spending public funds for renovation of airports that are scheduled to be privatized; 
(c) whether there is any option to recover such amount from the bidders of the said airports; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of Indian citizens who voluntarily surrendered their Indian citizenships during last five years, State-wise and year-wise, the reasons therefor;
(b) the details of countries whose citizenship have been acquired by such people in lieu of Indian citizenship, year-wise and State-wise details thereof; and
(c) the steps taken by Government to address the issue including any policy changes or other initiatives?

(a) the total number of Indians who have sought asylum in foreign countries during each of the last three years and the current year, country-wise;
(b) whether it is a fact that there has been an 800 per cent rise between 2021 and 2023 in the number of Indians seeking asylum in the United States, half of them being from Gujarat; and
(c) if so, the steps taken by Government to address the issue of Indians seeking asylum in foreign countries?

(a) whether Government is aware of the fact that nearly 5 crore people have had their Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) job cards deleted due to non-linking of Aadhaar with the bank accounts;
(b) the number of people whose MGNREGA cards have been deleted due to non-linking of Aadhaar with bank accounts, State-wise; and
(c) the list of MGNREGA workers who have been denied wages due to non-linking of Aadhaar with Bank accounts, State-wise?

(a) the percentage of rural households that currently have access to piped and safe drinking water connections as per the most recent available data;
(b) the major factors contributing to the inability to meet the target of providing tap water supply to every rural household by 2024;
(c) the long term plans for providing drinking water in areas without perennial water sources; and
(d) State-wise list of reported and certified connections?

(a) whether Government has proposed to develop Phase III of the eCourt Project for operation in various courts, including High Courts and District Courts across the country;
(b) if so, the State-wise details of progress made thereunder, including establishment of virtual benches of the High Courts;
(c) whether Government has conducted an assessment of usefulness of Phase I and Phase II in enabling citizens’ access to justice, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government has formulated any SOPs for Phase III, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?
